This manifest lists questions, spans, sha256 hashes and authored edits for the connected
memory evidence checks. The source text is fetched at the revisions pinned in
benchmarks/datasets/legal.py and benchmarks/datasets/memory.py, and it is checked against
the hashes here. The only source text kept in the manifest is the legal answer string of
each labelled span, which the legal fixtures already hold. No chat text is stored: BEAM
spans hold offsets and hashes.

Legal documents: privacy_qa/Keep.txt and privacy_qa/Viber Messenger.txt from the PrivacyQA
set, and contractnli/Kenway-NDA-Form-Blank.txt from ContractNLI. The files come from the
LegalBench-RAG mirror at https://huggingface.co/datasets/awinml/legalbench-rag, at revision
0263f7b2a9fb811f984ead05a0aa0d796a456124. PrivacyQA is MIT
(https://github.com/AbhilashaRavichander/PrivacyQA_EMNLP). ContractNLI is CC BY 4.0
(https://stanfordnlp.github.io/contract-nli/). The LegalBench-RAG code is MIT
(https://github.com/zeroentropy-ai/legalbenchrag).

Memory documents: sessions 1 and 3 of conversation 17 of BEAM, at
https://huggingface.co/datasets/Mohammadta/BEAM, at revision
3205395e897e7318c7b094ef4e6047b9b82dbb03. The data is under CC BY-SA 4.0, so the questions
and rubrics here keep that license. The BEAM code (https://github.com/mohammadtavakoli78/BEAM)
is MIT.

Builder: benchmarks/fixtures/builders/connected_memory.py. Run
"uv run python -m benchmarks.fixtures.builders.connected_memory" to rebuild manifest.json.
